    "md5": "a9db8f1058c6b44af6018c35f3bf3f89",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1816,
    "chunk_text": "ComBank celebrates pensioners with a dedicated event in Gampaha\n\nThe Commercial Bank of Ceylon reaffirmed its commitment to the welfare of senior citizens by organising a dedicated day to celebrate and honour pensioners. This special event was organised by the Bank\u2019s Retail Products Department together with the Bank\u2019s Gampaha Branch.\n\nThe event, held at the Royal Chance Palace Hotel, Gampaha, brought together more than 250 pensioners for a morning of health checks, learning, entertainment and fellowship.\n\nGuests included Government pensioners, Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) pensioners and Central Bank pensioners, who were treated to an engaging and informative programme. Among the highlights were a presentation on non-communicable diseases by a Government University Lecturer, a free medical health camp conducted in collaboration with Asiri Hospital \u2013 Kandy, and presentations by Commercial Bank on the financial facilities available to pensioners, including the Bank\u2019s Pension Loan product.\n\nParticipants were also able to apply for pension loans and obtain information on other financial services at the venue. The event concluded with a lively entertainment segment by two popular comedians, followed by snacks and lunch for all attendees.\n\nThe Bank said the event was organised to strengthen relationships with the senior citizen community and to promote financial wellbeing among pensioners in the Gampaha District.\n\nLion Brewery (Ceylon) PLC Reaffirms Commitment to Flood Resilience and Community Support in Biyagama\n\nJaffna Hindu College earns regional praise at AIA Healthiest Schools Competition\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
