    "md5": "9ed1050a00b3360826527d29522942ee",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1538,
    "chunk_text": "While there were quite a few who seemed interested in showing their keenness to make donations that Sunday, Fr. Asiri assessed that the second Sunday after the announcement will be the better day to see what kind of support there was for this, his first project in the new parish.\n\nHowever, the last two entries in the book of pledges were revealing, or even shocking. The difference of pledges was so stark that it was disturbing and they so upset him that it disturbed his sleep that night.\n\nIn fact, after seeing the last entry, he could vaguely remember the person who may have written that. A man in a well-worn shirt and a patched sarong who looked like he could do with some help himself.\n\nThat night, even as he fell asleep, he could not forget the one million rupee contribution pledged verses the fifty rupee contribution next to that and understandably he did not sleep well and dreamed badly. In the dream that he saw, there stood the church gleaming white with a procession of well-dressed people coming in procession but as they neared the church, the sky turned dark and rain poured down causing the paint to peel off and suddenly in front of the people approaching was a poor man holding a monetary note.\n\nWhile his normal wake up time was 5.00 a.m., disturbed by the dream and his thoughts, he was up by 3.00 the next morning. Not getting up but remaining in bed he contemplated the reality of the situation revealed through the contributions pledged. In fact, he was determined that he would act on it and not ignore it."
