    "md5": "60f19ff190630d1d3b6b84b614c72edc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1492,
    "chunk_text": "While his normal wake up time was 5.00 a.m., disturbed by the dream and his thoughts, he was up by 3.00 the next morning. Not getting up but remaining in bed he contemplated the reality of the situation revealed through the contributions pledged. In fact, he was determined that he would act on it and not ignore it.\n\nThe welcome from John was a smile in genuine surprise. \u201cCome in Father\u201d he said and pointed to a chair, the only one that was there while he himself kept standing.\n\nIn his conversation with John, Father Asiri found out that John was a former carpenter who had given up work after his wife had fallen and broken her leg three years ago, from which she had never fully recovered mostly due to lack of medical care, which in turn was due to the lack of money to take her for treatment. Reduced to charity through a few who was aware of John\u2019s situation, some of whom were those for whom he had done carpentry work on and off John had continued to look after his wife and manage his living without complaining. Though he was tempted to ask why he had pledged the fifty rupees for the church fund, Father did not, as John mentioned that someone had promised to give him money later in the month. This reminded Father of the Gospel story of a widow who put two copper coins in the temple till which earned Jesus\u2019 praise and as he left he allowed John to assume that this was one of his parish visits instead of a special visit prompted by an entry in the church fund book."
