    "chunk_text": "In his conversation with John, Father Asiri found out that John was a former carpenter who had given up work after his wife had fallen and broken her leg three years ago, from which she had never fully recovered mostly due to lack of medical care, which in turn was due to the lack of money to take her for treatment. Reduced to charity through a few who was aware of John\u2019s situation, some of whom were those for whom he had done carpentry work on and off John had continued to look after his wife and manage his living without complaining. Though he was tempted to ask why he had pledged the fifty rupees for the church fund, Father did not, as John mentioned that someone had promised to give him money later in the month. This reminded Father of the Gospel story of a widow who put two copper coins in the temple till which earned Jesus\u2019 praise and as he left he allowed John to assume that this was one of his parish visits instead of a special visit prompted by an entry in the church fund book.\n\nThough he met many of his parishioners after Mass as he normally did, none requested the withdrawal of their contribution.\n\nThanking God in his prayers that night for opening his eyes to the real needs of the parish, instead of his own perceptions of the needs, Father Asiri knew that Christmas for him and the parishioners will be a better one, a Christmas that would make the people feel that they found room in their hearts to help where help was needed and not allow the \u201cthere is no room at the inn\u201d to be the reality of the day.\n\nPsychosocial insights from the birth of Our Lord Jesus for a world striving to uphold the sanctity of human life\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
