    "chunk_size_bytes": 1924,
    "chunk_text": "The Jaffna International Trade Fair (JITF), Northern Sri Lanka\u2019s largest and most influential multitrade exhibition, will return for its 16th consecutive year from 23 to 25 January 2026 at the Muttraweli Ground in Jaffna. As the region\u2019s most established commercial platform, the fair continues to play a central role in advancing economic betterment, fostering business connectivity, and promoting technology-driven innovation across the Northern Province. Organised by Lanka Exhibition & Conference Services (LECS)\u2014Sri Lanka\u2019s leading exhibition and trade-show organiser and Presidential Award Winner in association with the Chamber of Commerce & Industries of Yarlpanam (CCIY)\u2014JITF has grown into one of the country\u2019s most anticipated annual events. LECS, known for its professionalism and decades-long industry expertise, ensures that JITF offers top-tier participation, wide national visibility, and a steady promotional reach throughout the Jaffna Peninsula. Its strong network and reputation continue to draw businesses, investors, and institutions that recognise the fair as a strategic gateway to the rapidly developing Northern market.\n\nJITF\u2019s strength lies in its wide-ranging sector representation, making it a central hub for innovation, trade, and commercial growth. The 2026 exhibition will feature an array of industries, including: Construction materials and machinery, Automobile, Consumer Products, Agriculture, Hotel Supplies, Apparel and machinery, Food, Beverage and Packaging, ICT, Financial Services, Education, Healthcare Products and Services, Emerging and specialised industries. This broad coverage ensures that the fair caters to both B2B and B2C audiences, attracting an impressive cross-section of stakeholders from multiple sectors. The exhibition provides an ideal environment for product launches, market testing, business matchmaking, and networking with key decision-makers."
  },
