    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ba61803d9938bb863cadecefd167f55e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1220,
    "chunk_text": "The NPP is duty-bound to honour the Social Contract of Political Accountability entered into with the people of SL. People in SL have discharged their part of the obligation by installing the NPP in power, and it is up to the NPP to fulfill its part of the obligation or prepare to face the wrath of the masses come next election.\u00a0 It requires them to ensure that the Rule of Law is established and implemented in a manner where everyone is equal in the eyes of the law, and no one, irrespective of whatever the reason, receives preferential treatment.\n\nThe President AKD is facing a mammoth challenge today, as never before, posed by the internal deficiencies and shortcomings of the NPP politicians. They are becoming increasingly conspicuous by the day. Their political implications could prove more damaging than any lapses in disaster management or the handling of the economic challenges faced by SL today. The NPP top leadership should devise a strategy and an action plan to groom its politicians to act with political maturity and finesse in their public lives, play leadership roles, and discharge their responsibilities effectively. They must be upskilled in many areas of competency that seem to be lacking."
