    "md5": "6b4a1ef595376455f694c862079c145d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1861,
    "chunk_text": "ComBank, CBA launch smart POS for SMEs\n\nCommercial Bank of Ceylon, in partnership with Ceylon Business Appliances (CBA), has introduced the \u2018PAX E700,\u2019 a new Android-powered smart Point-of-Sale (POS) device, aimed at empowering small and medium enterprises (SMEs) with advanced digital payment solutions.\n\nThe all-in-one device is designed to streamline operations, digitize transactions, and enhance the customer checkout experience by combining a traditional cash register with a modern payment terminal. It supports multiple payment methods, including Visa, MasterCard, UnionPay, and LankaPay, and offers connectivity via Wi-Fi, 4G, and LAN.\n\nS. Ganeshan, Deputy General Manager \u2013 Personal Banking at Commercial Bank, stated the launch aligns with the bank\u2019s commitment to the SME sector. \u201cWe are providing a cutting-edge digital tool that can play a pivotal role in helping businesses grow and thrive,\u201d he said, noting the device helps reduce operational costs and improve sales efficiency.\n\nRuwath Fernando, CEO of CBA, highlighted the partnership\u2019s role in advancing payment solutions in Sri Lanka. \u201cWe\u2019re excited to see how this innovative product will empower businesses to offer secure, efficient, and convenient payment services,\u201d he said. He added that the collaboration leverages Commercial Bank\u2019s financial services and CBA\u2019s technology expertise to support the country\u2019s digital transformation.\n\nCommercial Bank, the largest private sector lender and the biggest provider of credit to SMEs in Sri Lanka, serves as the acquiring partner for the new system.\n\nFACETS 2026 to unveil new era for Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery trade\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
