    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "First of all, let\u2019s take a look at her qualifications. The D\u00eepavasa reports her commitment to the monastic path immediately following her brother Mahinda\u2019s ordination:\n\nAt the same time Saghamitt\u00e2 began to exercise herself in the \u201cSikkh\u00e2 precepts.\u201d\n\nThen the D\u00eepavasa goes on about Sanghamitt\u00e2 Mah\u00e2ther\u00ee\u2019s Qualifications: the diplomatic mission was led by a highly qualified scholar:\n\nbahussut\u00e2 Sanghamitt\u00e2 chaabhi\u00f1\u00f1\u00e2 vicakkha\u00e2 catasso t\u00e2 bhikkhuniyo sabb\u00e2 ca bodhim \u00e2haru.\n\n\u201cand learned, wise Sanghamitt\u00e2 who was endowed with the six (extraordinary) faculties, these were the four Bhikkhun\u00ees who brought each a Bo branch (to this island).\u201d\n\nWhen you read the text, these two precise terms jump out. These are the terms used to describe her:\n\nBahussut\u00e2 (P\u00e2li: Bahu \u2013 much/many; sutta \u2013 discourse) translates to \u201cwell-versed in the Texts,\u201d confirming her scholarly command of the Tipitaka.\n\nShe then put a team of people together: Ther\u00ee Saghamitt\u00e2 was accompanied by a highly specialised group of eleven other nuns from Jambud\u00eepa: Uttar\u00e2, Vicakkha\u00e2, Hem\u00e2, Pas\u00e2dap\u00e2l\u00e2, Aggimitt\u00e2, D\u00e2sik\u00e2, Pheggu, Pabbat\u00e2, Matt\u00e2, Mall\u00e2, and Dhammad\u00e2siy\u00e2.\n\nTherik\u00e2 Saghamitt\u00e2 ca, Uttar\u00e2 ca Vicakkha\u00e2, Hem\u00e2 Pas\u00e2dap\u00e2l\u00e2 ca, Aggimitt\u00e2 ca D\u00e2sik\u00e2, Pheggu Pabbat\u00e2 Matt\u00e2, Mall\u00e2 ca Dhammad\u00e2siy\u00e2, et\u00e2 d\u00e2rika-bhikkhuniyo, Jambud\u00eep\u00e2 idh\u2019 \u00e2gat\u00e2. ..These young nuns came hither from Jambud\u00eepa to Lanka to establish the Bhikkhun\u00ee Order.\n\nThe D\u00eepavasa says they were experts in Vinaya and the Texts.\n\nThe Preparation of the Activator: Mahes\u00ee Anul\u00e2 Dev\u00ee Active Waiting and Self-Instruction\n\nWhile Sanghamitt\u00e2 Mah\u00e2ther\u00ee was selecting her team at the royal palace at P\u00e2aliputra in Jambud\u00eepa, an equally powerful, meticulous, preparation was happening in Sri Lanka.\n\nM\u00e2hesi Anul\u00e2 Dev\u00ee, sister-in-law of King Dev\u00e2napiya Tissa, did not wait passively, twiddling her thumbs."
