    "chunk_text": "When the ship finally arrived at Jambukola, it was not a meeting of strangers. It was the coming together of two strategic leaders.\n\nThe experiences of Sanghamitt\u00e2 Mah\u00e2ther\u00ee and Mahes\u00ee Anul\u00e2 Dev\u00ee are not dusty spiritual wall-flowers, bizarre statues, or grotesque artifacts. They are vibrant case studies in strategic foresight.\n\nThe facts presented above are based on the D\u00eepava\u1e43sa (Chapter XVIII) and the Mah\u00e2vasa (Chapters XVIII-XIX).\n\n(Don de Silva is a University Counsellor and Mentor, residing in the\n\nUK. He was a former director of the United Nations Environment\n\nProgramme (UNEP) and also a former director of the International\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
