    "md5": "bf89dd3dfa91f2ce5efec76122e8dc2d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1752,
    "chunk_text": "(b) Nature of the financial resources or other resources used to acquire, posses, own, control, have dominion in the aforestated property.\n\n(c) The manner in which the aforestated financial or other resources were earned, received or otherwise acquired.\n\n(e) If the aforestated properties being held in trust on behalf of any other person the name and the details necessary to identify and have access to such person.\n\n(f) If any other person derives or is due to derive any benefit from the aforestated property name and the details necessary to identify and have access to such person.\n\n(g) If answers to any one or more of the above questions is believed to be with any other person name and the details necessary to identify and have access to such person.\n\nOn 12 November 2025 the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development forwarded to the Governor of the Central Bank a communication issued by the Secretary of the Ministry of Justice and National Integration. The communication has to be forwarded to all CEOs or General Managers of Banks of which the majority of shareholding is either directly or otherwise held by the Secretary to the Treasury and all CEOs and General Managers of institutions recognized as engaging in finance business or as designated non-finance business.\n\nHowever, what is of grave concern is that the communication states that in terms of section 16 of the Act officers who receive information outside the institution\u2019s business must notify the designated authorities and that the failure to disclose such knowledge or information is a criminal offence.\n\nIt seems that the above requirement was not given adequate publicity by the Central Bank or the FIU or at seminars organized by various organisations."
