    "md5": "5915fde1acb2b21cb784088043b2a7dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1978,
    "chunk_text": "However, what is of grave concern is that the communication states that in terms of section 16 of the Act officers who receive information outside the institution\u2019s business must notify the designated authorities and that the failure to disclose such knowledge or information is a criminal offence.\n\nIt seems that the above requirement was not given adequate publicity by the Central Bank or the FIU or at seminars organized by various organisations.\n\nSimply because an individual or an entity has an expensive mansion or purchased a new car or engages in other life-style changes reflective of newly acquired wealth, is it possible to always assume that these represent the proceeds of crime even if there are unconfirmed rumors that the individual or concerned entity has engaged or is engaging in unlawful activities as defined in related legislation such as the Prevention of Money Laundering Act or the Financial Transactions Reporting Act or the Anti-Corruption Act? Section 34 of the PoC provides for the operation of various presumptions where the Court has to make a decision on a balance of probability\n\nUnderlying the allegation that something is represented to be the proceeds of crime is that there is proof that the individual or entity alleged to have ownership is the true \u2018beneficial owner\u2019. This is a cardinal aspect that deserves more serious consideration. A book by the author of this article entitled Beneficial Ownership: The Dynamics of Unmasking Beneficial Ownership in the Fight against Economic Crime is scheduled to be released in early January 2026 and this book sheds more light on some the complexities involved in enforcing the Proceeds of Crime Act.\n\nHow Fountain Caf\u00e9 tried to bag the Metropole chef after the Chairman enjoyed a sumptuous steak\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
