    "md5": "4ed768e5ba0c47aed3bce5660d460406",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "There is also a narrative that the Opposition Leader can never become President. Unfortunately, some opposition figures promote this idea for personal gain. Similar claims were once made about M.K. Stalin in Tamil Nadu, yet today he is Chief Minister. Sajith Premadasa faces continuous mudslinging. In the last presidential election, had it not been for Ranil Wickremesinghe dividing the vote between the UNP and SJB, Sajith Premadasa could well have been President today.\n\nEvery time Sajith is willing to move toward reconciliation, the UNP leadership attacks him. Under such circumstances, how can he trust them? He knows he will never be allowed to return to the UNP as long as Ranil Wickremesinghe is in control.\n\nQ: How do you assess the situation following Cyclone Ditwah in your districts?\n\nA:When in opposition, the NPP and JVP criticized every government after natural disasters, questioning their preparedness and relevance. This time, despite warnings from the Meteorological Department and international reports, timely action was not taken.\n\nWhen landslides occur, lives cannot be saved. But when floods were predicted, people in areas like Gampola and Kandy could have been evacuated. I personally visited Nuwara Eliya, Hatton, Lindula, and Ramboda and witnessed the devastation.\n\nNow the NPP/JVP, having come to power, are facing the consequences of their own criticisms. At a district meeting chaired by the President after the cyclone, I emphasized that people prefer to be rehoused in the same areas they lived in. However, decisions are delayed pending NBRO reports. What is the use of holding land while people continue to die?\n\nIndia has already provided funds to build houses for hill country communities, but previous governments failed to allocate land. If this government acts decisively, those funds can finally be utilized."
