    "chunk_size_bytes": 1754,
    "chunk_text": "Nawaloka Hospitals Colombo Marks Four Decades of Responsible, Patient Centered Healthcare\n\nColombo , For more than four decades, Nawaloka Hospitals PLC has played a vital role in Sri Lanka\u2019s healthcare landscape, guided by a steadfast commitment to safe, ethical, and patient-centred care. Growing in step with the nation\u2019s evolving healthcare needs, the institution has consistently worked to uphold clinical standards aligned with international best practice anchored in professional accountability, transparency, and public trust.\n\nNawaloka Hospitals delivers comprehensive healthcare services through a multidisciplinary, team-based model led by experienced medical professionals across a wide range of specialties. This coordinated approach ensures continuity of care, sound clinical decision-making, and patient safety throughout every stage of treatment.\n\nIn recent years, the Hospital has strengthened its clinical capabilities through the progressive integration of advanced and AI-supported medical technologies. These systems enhance diagnostics, laboratory processes, and clinical workflows supporting healthcare professionals, improving efficiency, and ensuring greater consistency and accuracy in patient outcomes.\n\nCommenting on the institution\u2019s journey, Dr. Jayantha Dharmadasa, Chairman of Nawaloka Hospitals PLC, said \u201cFor over 40 years, Nawaloka Hospitals has been guided by a simple but powerful principle responsibility to our patients and to the nation\u2019s healthcare system. Our focus has always been on ethical practice, clinical excellence, and continuous improvement. As medicine advances, we remain committed to adopting innovation responsibly, while preserving the trust placed in us by generations of Sri Lankans.\u201d"
  },
