    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a117b4e7e3174fb8a623fbbc77bf3548",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1649,
    "chunk_text": "SLT-Mobitel leads Lanka\u2019s 5G Digital Transformation\n\nMarking a major leap forward in the country\u2019s digital transformation journey, SLT-MOBITEL, the National ICT Solutions Provider, has made its 5G network publicly available, enabling Sri Lankans to experience the power and possibilities of next-generation connectivity.\n\nBeyond unprecedented speed and ultra-low latency, SLT-MOBITEL 5G represents a transformative ecosystem that will redefine how Sri Lankans learn, work, and lead their lifestyle. The technology has the potential to revolutionise key sectors such as education, healthcare, manufacturing, and enable innovation at scale. By accelerating digital inclusion and empowering enterprises, SLT-MOBITEL 5G will lay the foundation for a future-ready, knowledge-driven economy, positioning Sri Lanka to compete in the global digital landscape.\n\nAs part of this landmark chapter, SLT-MOBITEL hosted a 5G interactive experience at One Galle Face Mall (OGF), where the public experienced firsthand the promise of 5G and witnessed its potential in action. The SLT-MOBITEL 5G experience at OGF invited visitors to explore augmented (AR) and virtual reality (VR) applications, real-time gaming, and live speed demonstrations, showcasing the power of 5G. The event was attended by Deputy Minister of Digital Economy Eng. Eranga Weeraratne, Acting Secretary to Ministry of Digital Economy Waruna Sri Dhanapala, Chairman of SLT Group Dr. Mothilal De Silva, Board of Directors of SLT-MOBITEL, Chief Executive Officer of SLT Group Imantha Wijekoon, Chief Operating Officer of Mobitel Sudharshana Geeganage, and the Senior Management of SLT-MOBITEL."
  },
  {
