    "chunk_size_bytes": 728,
    "chunk_text": "If the government thinks Hiru or any other media institution disseminates false information to the detriment of its interests, legal avenues are available for it to seek redress. The police must not be used as a political tool to intimidate the media.\n\nThe government deserves the bad press it gets. The police have been reduced to a mere appendage of the JVP/NPP. Two of the NPP\u2019s Retired Police Collective members, namely former Senior DIG Ravi Seneviratne and former SSP Shani Abeysekera, have been appointed Secretary to the Public Security Ministry and CID Director, respectively. Absurd claims the police make in defence of the government remind us of Matilda, whose dreadful lies made one gasp and stretch one\u2019s eyes."
  },
