    "chunk_text": "Recent actions by the government and the public demonstrate notable resolve and commitment in responding to this crisis. However, given the scale of the disaster, particularly for a small island nation, recovery will be a demanding and complex process. As climate change is expected to increase both the frequency and intensity of similar events, reconstruction efforts must adopt a forward-looking approach. In this context, recovery should be guided by the principles of \u201cbuilding back better\u201d (B3), designed for future conditions rather than those of the past. Globally, this concept is becoming the norm.\n\n*The writer is a graduate of the Faculty of Engineering, University of Peradeniya. He has a Ph.D. degree from Colorado State University and is a Research Profess at Florida International University in the United States. He received the 2015 Norman Medal of the American Society of Civil Engineers for a technical paper that makes a definitive contribution in engineering.\u00a0 He was a member of the US National Committee which developed the 2014 National Climate Assessment."
