    "md5": "ae67d9d68490fa8e153e1bbcb78e982a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1942,
    "chunk_text": "Plenty of excitement to welcome 2026\n\nThe city of Colombo, especially Galle Face, has certainly been buzzing with excitement, since the start of the festive season!\n\nThe area around Galle Face Green has an awesome carnival atmosphere, and beautifully lit up, as well \u2026 including food stalls, music, and, of course, crowds.\n\nThe city\u2019s got a great vibe, especially if you like food, shopping, or just soaking in the atmosphere.\n\nWith the year 2025 coming to an end, at midnight, 31st night revellers are ready to usher in 2026 \u2026 dancing the night away!\n\nThey have a choice, indeed, with most venues in the city ready to welcome the New Year \u2026 in style!\n\nThe ultimate New Year\u2019s Eve bash, in the opinion of many, especially Colombo\u2019s A-list crowd, is going to be \u2018Dancing Through the Decades\u2019, at the City of Dreams, Cinnamon Life, Colombo.\n\nAccording to reports coming my way, Cinnamon Life is hosting the most epic party of the year \u2013 on December 31st.\n\nThe Lumina Ballroom will be transformed into a time machine, taking you on a musical journey through the decades.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s finest artistes will be around to provide star-class entertainment, and the lineup includes the sensational Sohan Weerasinghe, the charismatic Rukshan Perera, the electrifying Damian Wikramatillake, the fabulous Falan Andrea, the stunning Corrine Almeida, the legendary Geoffrey Fernando, and the versatile Clifford Richards.\n\nThe bands Flame and AROH will ignite the stage, while the incomparable Kumar de Silva will keep the crowd entertained \u2026 as the compere.\n\nThe action is from 8:00 PM onwards and \u2018Dancing Through The Decades\u2019 will culminate in a dazzling countdown to welcome 2026, with a sumptuous gourmet buffet and traditional Sri Lankan breakfast to follow.\n\nWith an incredible lineup of artistes and a night full of music, dance, and celebration, it\u2019s going to be a fantastic way to bid farewell to 2025 and welcome 2026."
