    "chunk_text": "\u201cReaching 85 years is not just a milestone\u2014it is a responsibility,\u201d said Dr. De Soysa. \u201cA responsibility to every parent, every child, and every stakeholder who has trusted Velona across generations. My commitment is to honour my grandfather\u2019s legacy by raising our standards of care, safety, and innovation, while giving Velona the wings to fly beyond our shores.\u201d\n\nAs part of its 85-year celebrations, Velona is entering an exciting new chapter in feminine care with the launch of Venus by Velona, a super-premium sanitary napkin range designed specifically for Sri Lankan women. Offering high-absorbency solutions for Regular and Heavy Flow needs, Venus also introduces Sri Lanka\u2019s first-ever Teen/ Tween sanitary napkin, thoughtfully created to support young girls with comfort, dignity, and confidence. Manufactured to international standards and offered at accessible price points, Venus reflects Velona\u2019s mission to empower women at every stage of life.\n\nTrue to its values, Velona is marking this milestone not only with innovation, but with compassion. In response to recent floods, the company is extending targeted CSR initiatives, distributing diapers, essential items, and care packs to affected children, families, and orphanages across the island\u2014ensuring that even in times of hardship, care reaches those who need it most.\n\nLooking ahead, Velona is broadening its definition of care to include knowledge and emotional support for parents. Acknowledging the growing need for awareness around learning and behavioural differences such as ADHD, dyslexia, and autism, the brand will soon launch a digital education series designed to equip families with practical guidance and reassurance as they support children with special needs."
