    "md5": "a2efcf9260de693e9ff437dc0f7e5b99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1832,
    "chunk_text": "According to informed Tamil circles close to Douglas Devananda, the  EPDP leader had received the 9mm pistol in July 2001 as part of a mini-arsenal provided to the EPDP for protection against the LTTE. The cache consisted of nineteen  T-56 assault rifles  and six 9 mm pistols. Subsequently the EPDP had been asked to hand over  the firearms issued to them twice.\n\nThe second occasion was after the war ended conclusively following the military defeat of the LTTE in May 2009. The EPDP had returned the arms on a staggered basis to the defence ministry.The firearm in question had also been returned to the defence ministry. If the gun had  really  been in Madush\u2019s possession, then it was more likely that the \u201clapse\u201dwas by the \u201cdefence sector\u201d and not the EPDP opined informed Tamil sources.\n\nAnother possibility is that an EPDP cadre may have sold the firearm to the underworld without Devananda\u2019s knowledge. Several cadres of other Tamil groups had lso sold their firearms to the underworld after the war ended. Even if this were tru, it is the EPDP leader Devananda who has to shoulder responsibility as the  arms had been given to him under certain conditions and guarantees.\n\nAccording to these Tamil circles close to the EPDP, former minister Devananda had clearly furnished  details of the various arms given to the EPDP by the Defence ministry. Devananda however had insisted during the interrogation that his statement should be recorded in Tamil. He had pointed out that Tamil was his mother tongue and also an official language. Therefore he was entitled to have his statement recorded in Tamil as his Constitutional right. The CID officers who quizzed Devananda were unable to record the  statement in  Tamil. It is expected that arrangements would be made to  enable the statement to be recorded in Tamil."
  },
